<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 23 March, from 1540 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1540 <span class="tih-ago">486 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Waltham Abbey surrenders, the last English monastery to close</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Augustinian abbey at Waltham in Essex was surrendered to Henry VIII's commissioners. It completed the Dissolution of the Monasteries, which transferred vast church lands to the Crown.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/virginia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virginia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1775 <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Patrick Henry declares 'Give me liberty, or give me death!'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Second Virginia Convention in Richmond, Henry urged the colony to raise a militia against Britain. The convention agreed, and fighting began at Lexington four weeks later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1801 <span class="tih-ago">225 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tsar Paul I murdered in St Michael's Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Conspiring officers killed the erratic Tsar in his bedroom in St Petersburg. His son Alexander I, aware of the plot, succeeded him and later led Russia against Napoleon.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1919 <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mussolini founds the Fasci di Combattimento in Milan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Benito Mussolini gathered veterans and nationalists in Piazza San Sepolcro to found a new movement. Its blackshirts helped him take power in 1922, and Fascism became a model for Hitler.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascism">Fascism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1933 <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Reichstag passes the Enabling Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With communists barred and others intimidated, the German parliament allowed Hitler's cabinet to make laws without it. Only the Social Democrats voted against, and the dictatorship had a legal basis.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1965 <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gemini 3 makes the first crewed Gemini flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gus Grissom and John Young flew three orbits and became the first astronauts to change their spacecraft's orbit. The Gemini programme prepared the techniques for Apollo.</p></div></li></ol>
